{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/824452-resource-merit","id":824452,"title":"Resource Merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-05T10:55:43-08:00","id":824452,"title":"Resource Merit","content":"Hi everyone.<br /> <br /> Just wanted to see how other GM's handled the resource merit. Do u assign a set dollar figure or attach a set lifestyle to the merit dots?<br /> <br /> Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11109-nemesis","name":"Nemesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T13:00:17-08:00","id":824534,"title":"","content":"I go with a general lifestyle. 1 dot is enough to pay your bills with a little left over to spend here and there. 2 is a solid middle-class lifestyle. 3 is moderately wealthy. 4 is very wealthy. 5 is filthy rich. What each of those categories means is also dependent on the context of the setting - what's considered middle class in say Silicon Valey would easily be considered filthy rich in many other parts of the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T17:48:33-08:00","id":824708,"title":"","content":"Well, I just used it as a measure of what you could buy at any given poitn in time. In theory, you could have a lavish lifestyle, but no merits to back it up. I only worried about what you could actually get in the course of the game.<br /> <br /> I also used resources as a measure of equipment bonuses. Need a really fast computer? You need Resources 3. Bonus from clothes or other social status symbols? 1/2 resource dots rounded up. ETc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T11:33:31-08:00","id":825022,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input guys/ do you temporary remove resource dots after purchases or leave it be as part of their lifestyle <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11109-nemesis","name":"Nemesis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T11:44:45-08:00","id":825030,"title":"","content":"I just use the rules as written. Once per chapter, your character can procure an item at her Resources level or lower, without issue. An item one Availability above her Resources reduces her effective Resources by one dot for a full month, since she has to rapidly liquidate funds. She can procure items two Availability below her Resources without limit (within reason).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T12:25:18-08:00","id":825055,"title":"","content":"We play Resources a little different:<br /> 1 low class<br /> 2 middle class<br /> 3 high class<br /> 4 one of the wealthiest in the town<br /> 5 one of the wealthiest in the country<br /> 6+ one of the wealthiest in the world<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10749,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10749-skydiver","user":"skydiver","date":". 02-06-2016, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10749-skydiver","name":"skydiver","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T15:34:10-08:00","id":825127,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there a fairly recent attempt by a prominent poster to hash out a set of &quot;crunchier&quot; Resource houserules? <br /> <br /> ...wait, no, not recent, exactly. A bit before the B&amp;S was released?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T10:55:05-08:00","id":825471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/824452-resource-merit?p=825127#post825127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't there a fairly recent attempt by a prominent poster to hash out a set of &quot;crunchier&quot; Resource houserules?<br /> <br /> ...wait, no, not recent, exactly. A bit before the B&amp;S was released?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/701015-resources-as-a-condition\"><b>this</b></a> might be thread you're talking about.<br /> <br /> Also, GMC has a list of Services and Equipment with the expected Availability on pages 234 and 235. The same chapter also lists several pieces of equipment and how they are used. You can find the same list of Services on pages 278 and 279 of CoD. As a bonus, CoD has a special system for building your own equipment on pages 100 to 103.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}